-- ============================================================================
-- FIDELITY 4: § 14 countersignature — too simple
--
-- Our type: Beslutning(kongelig: Bool, minister_underskrift: Bool, ansvarlig: String)
-- The text: "een eller flere ministres medunderskrift" — ONE OR MORE.
--
-- Multiple ministers can co-sign. Our type uses a single String.
-- This matters because responsibility follows the signature.
-- If three ministers co-sign, all three are responsible.
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F4: § 14 countersignature allows MULTIPLE ministers ---")
@ print("Text: 'een eller flere ministres medunderskrift'")
@ print("Our type: ansvarlig: String (single minister)")
@ print("Reality: multiple ministers can co-sign → multiple responsible")
@ print("Fix: ansvarlige: List(String)")
@ print("Severity: STRUCTURAL — changes responsibility analysis")
@ print("")

-- ============================================================================
-- FIDELITY 5: § 19 military force — Forsvar/Angreb binary is too coarse
--
-- The text says: "mod riget rettet angreb" — armed attack DIRECTED AT
-- THE REALM. Not just any military conflict. Self-defense is specifically
-- about attacks ON Denmark.
--
-- Our binary ForsvarModAngreb | AndenMilitærMagt loses this directionality.
-- A Danish military action abroad to protect citizens is neither
-- Forsvar (not attacked at home) nor Angreb (not aggression).
-- The constitution actually has a gap here.
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F5: § 19 military — directionality lost ---")
@ print("Text: 'forsvar mod et vaebnet angreb mod riget'")
@ print("  → defense against armed attack DIRECTED AT the Realm")
@ print("Our encoding: MilitaerMagtbrug = ForsvarModAngreb | AndenMilitaerMagt")
@ print("Missing: attacks AGAINST Denmark specifically")
@ print("Lost scenario: military action abroad (rescue, peacekeeping)")
@ print("  → not Forsvar (not attacked at home)")
@ print("  → not Angreb (not aggression)")
@ print("  → constitutional gap in the original text!")
@ print("Severity: STRUCTURAL — binary encoding reveals real gap in constitution")
@ print("")

-- ============================================================================
-- FIDELITY 6: § 29 — three requirements + exclusion, not four requirements
--
-- The text: "enhver, som har dansk indfodsret, fast bopael i riget og
--            har naaet valgretsalderen, MEDMINDRE vedkommende er umyndiggjort"
--
-- Structure: 3 positive requirements + 1 negative exclusion (medmindre = unless)
-- Our code: har_valgret(indfoedsret, fast_bopael, valgretsalder, myndig)
--           → treats all 4 as positive requirements
--
-- The text uses DEFAULT LOGIC: you HAVE suffrage if 3 conditions met,
-- UNLESS you are incapacitated. This should be a | rule with | exception.
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F6: § 29 structure is default + exception, not 4 conditions ---")
@ print("Text: '...indfodsret, fast bopael...valgretsalderen, MEDMINDRE umyndiggjort'")
@ print("Structure: 3 positive conditions + 'unless' exclusion")
@ print("Our code: 4 boolean parameters treated equally")
@ print("Better encoding in Futuruna's default logic:")
@ print("  | har_valgret(p) -> True under p.indfodsret, p.bopael, p.alder")
@ print("  | exception umyndiggoerelse har_valgret(p) -> False under p.umyndiggjort")
@ print("This is exactly what default logic is FOR.")
@ print("Severity: STRUCTURAL — misses opportunity to demonstrate default logic")
@ print("")

-- ============================================================================
-- FIDELITY 7: § 29 stk. 2 — voting age history not captured
--
-- We set nuvaerende_valgretsalder = 18.
-- But the 1953 text set it at 23. It was lowered by referendum:
--   1953: 23 (original)
--   1961: 21 (referendum)
--   1971: 20 (referendum)
--   1978: 18 (referendum)
--
-- Each change required a referendum per § 29 stk. 2.
-- The constitution doesn't say "18" — it says "the age that won
-- the referendum per the law of 25 March 1953."
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F7: § 29 voting age — we hardcode 18, text says 'referendum result' ---")
@ print("Constitutional text: 'den, som har opnaaet flertal ved folkeafstemning'")
@ print("History of referendum-locked changes:")
@ print("  1953: 23 (original)")
@ print("  1961: 21 (referendum)")
@ print("  1971: 20 (referendum)")
@ print("  1978: 18 (referendum)")
@ print("Our code: = nuvaerende_valgretsalder = 18 (hardcoded)")
@ print("The constitution doesn't say '18' — it says 'the referendum result'")
@ print("Severity: KOSMETISK — correct value, wrong provenance")
@ print("")

